NNAAMMEE
     sslloowwccggii — a FastCGI to CGI wrapper server

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     sslloowwccggii [--ddvv] [--pp _p_a_t_h] [--ss _s_o_c_k_e_t] [--tt _t_i_m_e_o_u_t] [--UU _u_s_e_r] [--uu _u_s_e_r]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     sslloowwccggii is a server which implements the FastCGI Protocol to execute CGI
     scripts.  FastCGI was designed to overcome the CGI protocol's scalability
     and resource sharing limitations.  While CGI scripts need to be forked
     for every request, FastCGI scripts can be kept running and handle many
     HTTP requests.

     sslloowwccggii is a simple server that translates FastCGI requests to the CGI
     protocol.  It executes the requested CGI script and translates its output
     back to the FastCGI protocol.

     Modern web frameworks and web applications usually come with the capabil‐
     ity to run as FastCGI servers.  sslloowwccggii is not intended for these appli‐
     cations.

     sslloowwccggii opens a socket at _/_v_a_r_/_w_w_w_/_r_u_n_/_s_l_o_w_c_g_i_._s_o_c_k, owned by www:www,
     with permissions 0660.  It will then chroot(8) to _/_v_a_r_/_w_w_w and drop priv‐
     ileges to user "www".

     The options are as follows:

     --dd      Do not daemonize.  If this option is specified, sslloowwccggii will run
             in the foreground and log to stderr.

     --pp _p_a_t_h
             chroot(2) to _p_a_t_h.  A _p_a_t_h of _/ effectively disables the chroot.

     --ss _s_o_c_k_e_t
             Create and bind to alternative local socket at _s_o_c_k_e_t.

     --tt _t_i_m_e_o_u_t
             Terminate the request after _t_i_m_e_o_u_t seconds instead of the de‐
             fault 120 seconds.  The CGI script is left to run but its stan‐
             dard input, output and error will be closed.

     --UU _u_s_e_r
             Change the owner of _/_v_a_r_/_w_w_w_/_r_u_n_/_s_l_o_w_c_g_i_._s_o_c_k to _u_s_e_r and its
             primary group instead of the default www:www.

     --uu _u_s_e_r
             Drop privileges to _u_s_e_r instead of default user www and chroot(8)
             to the home directory of _u_s_e_r.

     --vv      Enable more verbose (debug) logging.

